Adapted (src/gapcourt/itu_adapter.py). Each function below is the reference function with only the listed changes. Tests run the
vendored original and the adapted version on the same input and compare outputs (tests/test_itu_adapter.py):

  chunk_text           unchanged logic; the default chunk size (256 words) and overlap (30) are inlined from server/config.py
                       instead of read from the pydantic settings object.
  infer_source_type    unchanged. infer_country: unchanged. _strip_html: unchanged. build_metadata: unchanged.
  embed_texts          unchanged logic (batches of 16, 2,000-character pre-truncation, one-at-a-time fallback, 4,000-character
                       last resort). The `ollama` package is imported lazily and the client can be passed in, so the function
                       can be tested without a server. A failure of the last resort is raised as EmbedderUnavailable with a plain
                       message.
  _parse_pdf           the PyMuPDF path only. The docling path is removed (out of scope for this entry, not installed).
  KnowledgeBase        reduced to ChromaStore: add, search, count, stats and reset over named collections with cosine distance
                       and telemetry off. `chromadb` is imported lazily. Collections are named by the caller (kb_uae, kb_global,
                       kb_framework) instead of the reference names kb_main, kb_decisions, kb_framework, kb_usecase; ids are the
                       stable chunk ids of this repository instead of random UUIDs. The reference search_by_* helpers and the
                       decision store are not used.

Not used: ingest_directory, ingest_usecase_docs, ingest_framework_definitions, the CLI, the agents, the game engine.
The chunk boundaries and locators of this repository (src/gapcourt/chunking.py) are not the reference chunker's: the reference
chunker splits by word count and loses article locators, so it is kept for parity only and is not used to build the knowledge base.
